# Retail data (port/docs/retail-eu-plan.md, R3): the radio screen with the European discs, as the European
# code has it. (1) SubScreenExec sets four shared id tables of ss_cmmn.dat (pesetas, main menu, etc.,
# background) for every sub screen and hides them for the radio screen (open_flag 0x20), whose IdSub has
# 128 units; the European tables are larger and the radio's own units, the dark bar behind the subtitle
# among them, found no room ("IDSystem::set() work full"). The European SubScreenExec (main.dol
# 0x8005a920) does not set them for the radio screen, the European SsTermMain::init no main menu either.
# (2) The European radio table (ss_term.dat sub-file 9, 78 units instead of 46) has three more picture
# groups, 0x15..0x17, at the partner's picture; the European init hides them (0x16 not for call 14) and
# OpeMesMove switches them, and 0x12, at a frame of calls 13, 14, 15 and 17. Without (2) they lay over
# Hunnigan as soon as (1) gave them room (device and PC, 27.10.2026). Found with port/tools/retail_code.py
# in the European Sscrn.rel (SsTermMain::init, OpeMesMove; frames from its data section 20 +0x1200).
# Nothing changes with the debug build's discs. A port patch for retail data.
